WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:01.290
alive as chalk-lined phantoms.

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:05.530
Picture this: You’re out driving, visiting
the more rural towns of your home country.

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:11.760
It’s been a long trip, hours at a time or
sometimes full days spent on the open road,

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.259
with brief stops taken only for gas and snacks.

00:00:15.259 --> 00:00:19.950
Every time you hit the next town, you stop
for the night, maybe book a day or two at

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:21.450
a local hotel to rest.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.900
Then, you’re right back out on the road
again.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:28.040
It’s been a little while since you left
the last town, and it’s starting to get

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.040
late.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:33.470
The sun is dipping behind the horizon, and
pretty soon it’ll be night again.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:37.480
You don’t think it’s a good idea to keep
driving all through the night until tomorrow,

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.130
you need to sleep.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:43.440
The one problem is, you don’t know the highway
you’re on all that well, and the people

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.180
at the last town didn’t mention there being
anywhere else to stay for at least a few more

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.180
miles.

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:53.989
But then you turn on the radio, accidentally
tuning in to some kind of locally produced

00:00:53.989 --> 00:00:55.230
tourism ad.

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:59.290
Through the airwaves and the ever-growing
evening darkness, you hear:

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:04.830
“Welcome to Chalkland, a nice rural town
with a population who just can’t bear to

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:05.830
leave.

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:10.180
Located just off the freeway, you’ll find
our town is filled with all sorts of colorful

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:13.890
folks, who love nothing more than to greet
new faces.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:19.330
From the moment you arrive, you’ll see firsthand
the Chalkland locals’ love for art and expression,

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:23.970
and we even encourage our younger residents
to get in on the fun and let their creative

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:24.970
flair show!

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:29.280
Chalkland, once you’re here, you just won’t
be able to leave.”

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:30.280
Chalkland?

00:01:30.280 --> 00:01:35.200
You’ve never heard of the place; it wasn’t
on any maps when you planned your route, and

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.950
it doesn’t even show up on your car’s
GPS.

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:42.260
And what’s more, the people at the last
town you visited never said anything about

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:46.860
it, they said the nearest neighboring city
was much, much further away.

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:47.890
Did they lie?

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:51.280
Why wouldn’t they tell you that this other
town was closer?

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:56.360
You spot a road sign up ahead, pointing towards
the turning for Chalkland, and decide to try

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:57.360
your chances.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.409
A good night’s rest and you’ll be back
on the road… or so you think.

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:06.000
In any small town, there are bound to be secrets.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.709
Local legends, ghost stories, even grudges
between families that have lived there for

00:02:10.709 --> 00:02:12.249
generations.

00:02:12.249 --> 00:02:17.109
No matter how friendly and unassuming a place
might seem on the surface, there’s always

00:02:17.109 --> 00:02:20.810
bound to be something that people just don’t
talk about.

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:27.719
The township of Chalkland, otherwise known
as SCP-277, is no exception, hiding a fair

00:02:27.719 --> 00:02:30.239
few secrets of its own.

00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:34.739
Although the locals don’t know it, they
are living their seemingly ordinary lives

00:02:34.739 --> 00:02:37.349
under constant surveillance.

00:02:37.349 --> 00:02:42.030
Operatives of the SCP Foundation have been
integrated among the townsfolk, embedded within

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:47.169
the civilian population to monitor some of
the strange happenings going on in this otherwise

00:02:47.169 --> 00:02:48.169
normal town.

00:02:48.169 --> 00:02:53.880
So, why not take a walk with us through main
street, down the avenues of Chalkland, as

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:58.680
we draw your attention to some of the mysteries
of SCP-277.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:04.159
The first thing you’ll probably notice as
you stroll around town are all the chalk drawings.

00:03:04.159 --> 00:03:08.949
They’re everywhere, on the sidewalks and
the outer walls of buildings, scribbled on

00:03:08.949 --> 00:03:11.439
trash cans and houses.

00:03:11.439 --> 00:03:15.739
Practically every playground in town has been
turned into an urban art installation for

00:03:15.739 --> 00:03:18.169
these colorful children’s drawings.

00:03:18.169 --> 00:03:21.120
Not all that weird at first glance, right?

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:25.040
Perhaps it’s a good thing that the town
encourages its kids to express themselves

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.930
by having them draw all over the town with
chalk.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:33.049
But these images coating the town, on every
street corner and alleyway, they weren’t

00:03:33.049 --> 00:03:35.010
drawn with chalk.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:40.489
These apparitions, found throughout the area
of SCP-277, might look like harmless art.

00:03:40.489 --> 00:03:44.069
But not one of them was created in the way
you might expect.

00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:47.959
Little Timmy didn’t spend a few minutes
on his hands and knees, dragging a lump of

00:03:47.959 --> 00:03:49.409
chalk over the concrete.

00:03:49.409 --> 00:03:54.930
Oh no, the drawings found around Chalkland
seem to be projected directly from the minds

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:57.079
of the town’s children.

00:03:57.079 --> 00:04:02.729
All their thoughts, their wild and unfiltered
imaginations, have somehow been plastered

00:04:02.729 --> 00:04:05.920
all over every surface you can find.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:12.299
The Foundation calls these images instances
of SCP-277-1, with almost all of them appearing

00:04:12.299 --> 00:04:14.859
as figures ‘drawn’ in white outlines.

00:04:14.859 --> 00:04:16.630
Creepy, isn’t it?

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:18.350
Like part of a crime scene.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:22.940
Luckily, some of these projections take the
form of beanstalks, spaceships, anything from

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:25.750
the imagination of the child manifesting them.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:32.690
An instance of SCP-277-1 doesn’t possess
any physical form or any substantial three-dimensional

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:38.470
body, and the size, shape, style, and complexity
of each ‘drawing’ varies, all depending

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:40.530
on the child that creates them.

00:04:40.530 --> 00:04:45.720
Additionally, it’s only children that have
the capability to produce these images, anyone

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:50.130
over the age of pubescence is completely unable
to do so.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:54.500
As for how exactly the children of Chalkland
create SCP-277-1 instances?

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:59.010
Well, most of the time they aren’t even
aware that they’re projecting their thoughts

00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:01.810
into the form of these anomalous drawings.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:05.890
It’s an entirely unconscious and involuntary
process.

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:10.940
It’s hard for the SCP Foundation to put
an exact number on the number of children

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:14.900
in Chalkland, given the sheer size of the
town and its population.

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:21.730
So, predicting the exact number of active
instances of SCP-277-1s at any one time is

00:05:21.730 --> 00:05:25.100
pretty tricky, if not downright unfeasible.

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:29.930
The Foundation agents embedded among the townsfolk
have been able to confirm that these drawings

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:36.910
or projections are capable of interacting
with fellow SCP-277-1 instances, while physical

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:41.780
objects can pass through them without causing
or sustaining any form of damage.

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:47.570
It is due to this factor that the children
living in SCP-277 can often be seen playing

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:52.890
with their chalk projections, and the existence
of these living drawings is viewed as a totally

00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:57.150
normal and everyday occurrence by the adult
residents of Chalkland.

00:05:57.150 --> 00:06:03.320
In fact, you ask anyone who grew up living
in SCP-277, any lifelong local born and raised

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:07.820
in Chalkland, and they will tell you that
the living chalk projections of the town’s

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:11.760
children have existed as long as the town
itself has.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:17.800
According to the claims of the older residents,
SCP-277-1 instances have been appearing in

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:24.950
Chalkland for years and years, dating all
the way back to when SCP-277 was first colonized,

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.460
and the earliest settlers arrived in the town.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:32.480
However, the Foundation isn’t so sure that
these claims are one hundred percent accurate.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:38.440
For one, they can’t even find a single record
of SCP-277 existing before the 2000s.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:42.710
Even those living in neighboring towns refuse
to believe that Chalkland is a real place

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:44.140
that exists.

00:06:44.140 --> 00:06:49.530
Adding to the mystery surrounding the town
of SCP-277 is the fact that all of its inhabitants

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:55.330
also don’t seem to exist, or at least have
no official record of their existence anywhere

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:56.410
else.

00:06:56.410 --> 00:07:02.290
According to tests conducted by the Foundation,
the dental, DNA, and fingerprint data of everyone

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:08.740
living in SCP-277 don’t match any recorded
persons on national population databases.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:10.170
And on top of that?

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:15.960
None of the Chalkland residents have any memories
of living anywhere else other than the mysterious

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:19.460
town, or ever having traveled anywhere outside
it either.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:25.530
No vacations, road trips, not even as much
as a visit to relatives in the next town over.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:30.860
Naturally, before they implanted covert agents
among the locals, the SCP Foundation’s initial

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:36.060
attempt to contain SCP-277 was to evacuate
the civilian population.

00:07:36.060 --> 00:07:40.480
The plan was to remove the people from the
vicinity of the town, relocate them, and then

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:43.620
assess the local area’s anomalous properties.

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:48.340
What was it about that specific town that
caused the chalk projections to manifest?

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:52.460
Why were none of the residents’ details
anywhere on the national databases?

00:07:52.460 --> 00:07:57.730
And how could a single one of them never have
once left the confines of Chalkland?

00:07:57.730 --> 00:08:00.590
Evacuate and assess, that was the goal.

00:08:00.590 --> 00:08:04.990
But naturally, things weren’t as simple
in practice.

00:08:04.990 --> 00:08:09.680
Multiple failed evacuation attempts were made,
with some unforeseen incidents causing the

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:11.490
operations to go awry.

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:16.490
In an attempt to combat this, the SCP Foundation
tried to vary the specific details of its

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:21.620
evacuation strategy each time, but even then,
they couldn’t get the people out of the

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:22.620
town.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:27.580
What was perhaps far stranger, was that every
time the Foundation attempted a new evacuation,

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:34.419
the civilians living in SCP-277 denied having
any memories of the earlier, failed evacuations.

00:08:34.419 --> 00:08:38.559
There was so much disbelief in the occurrence
of these prior evacuation attempts that it

00:08:38.559 --> 00:08:42.699
caused the Foundation to question if these
attempts even took place.

00:08:42.699 --> 00:08:47.709
The only record of the failed evacuations
existing, were in their own files.

00:08:47.709 --> 00:08:53.079
On the odd occasion that Foundation operatives
were able to get one or two residents of SCP-277

00:08:53.079 --> 00:08:58.019
far enough away from the town, they learned
it was an exercise in futility.

00:08:58.019 --> 00:09:02.050
After spending any longer than a few brief
minutes outside the borders of Chalkland,

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:05.680
a resident would suffer some sort of violent
incident.

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:10.139
The exact nature of what would happen to them
has been redacted, however, we know for a

00:09:10.139 --> 00:09:13.230
fact they weren’t killed just by leaving
the town.

00:09:13.230 --> 00:09:19.740
Shortly after, these evacuated civilians would
be found back within SCP-277, with no memory

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:21.889
of ever having left the town.

00:09:21.889 --> 00:09:26.200
But what was causing all of these attempted
evacuations to fail?

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:29.150
What exactly was preventing the townsfolk
from leaving?

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:36.319
Well, the answers to these questions may be
found in a unique instance of SCP-277-1, which

00:09:36.319 --> 00:09:40.699
are far more actively hostile versions of
the chalk drawings that were collectively

00:09:40.699 --> 00:09:48.980
given the designation SCP-277-1-R.
These instances first came about some time

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:52.720
before the Foundation started attempting to
evacuate Chalkland.

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:57.529
One of their agents, undercover within the
town and monitoring anomalous activity, spotted

00:09:57.529 --> 00:10:02.820
a seemingly standard SCP-277-1 projection,
in the shape of a rabbit.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:07.301
It wasn’t a drawing that had been noticed
previously, so wasn’t present in any earlier

00:10:07.301 --> 00:10:08.889
reports coming out of SCP-277.

00:10:08.889 --> 00:10:13.649
But yet, there it was, at the local library.

00:10:13.649 --> 00:10:18.300
None of the town’s children admitted to
being responsible for casting this new projection.

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:22.380
Unusual, but not uncommon - after all, they
are kids.

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:25.569
Think about it, we’re sure that as a kid
you might have done something that you didn’t

00:10:25.569 --> 00:10:27.800
fess up to when a grown-up asked you.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:32.269
Granted, you probably never cast a psychic
projection onto a library though.

00:10:32.269 --> 00:10:37.660
The Foundation agents within SCP-277 knew
that the instances of the chalk drawings could

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:42.480
often be good indicators of the psychological
state of the child that manifested them, so

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:49.069
they aimed to keep an eye out for any further
SCP-227-1-R rabbits with a matching drawing

00:10:49.069 --> 00:10:50.069
style.

00:10:50.069 --> 00:10:53.220
Turns out, the agents found plenty more of
these rabbits.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:59.699
Before long, sightings of SCP-227-1-R instances
had tripled in frequency since that first

00:10:59.699 --> 00:11:01.360
one appeared at the library.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:07.720
But what was it that made these projections
different from the regular SCP-277-1 chalk

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:08.720
drawings?

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:13.450
Well, Agent Davis of the SCP Foundation witnessed
a cluster of these rabbit projections across

00:11:13.450 --> 00:11:15.009
the street from a diner.

00:11:15.009 --> 00:11:20.249
They were silently watching people or cars
that passed by at a nearby intersection; the

00:11:20.249 --> 00:11:22.769
rabbits didn’t play like the other sketches.

00:11:22.769 --> 00:11:25.750
Suddenly, the agent heard a scream from a
little girl.

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:30.379
She had been playing with her own chalk drawing
that took the shape of a pony with wings.

00:11:30.379 --> 00:11:34.740
Agent Davis turned around to see one of the
rabbits attacking the little girl’s sketch,

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:40.600
practically consuming the drawing thanks to
instances of SCP-277-1 being able to interact

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:41.600
with each other.

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:46.689
At the same time, the attack seemed to be
causing the girl to suffer some form of seizure.

00:11:46.689 --> 00:11:51.399
All around, the rest of the rabbits were doing
the same, seeking out other chalk drawings

00:11:51.399 --> 00:11:55.579
and devouring them, tearing them apart and
causing the children that had created their

00:11:55.579 --> 00:12:00.389
own SCP-277-1s to suffer the same seizure.

00:12:00.389 --> 00:12:05.199
Ultimately, any child who had their projection
attacked by a rabbit collapsed soon after,

00:12:05.199 --> 00:12:10.309
and slipped into a coma, with attempts to
awaken them proving unsuccessful.

00:12:10.309 --> 00:12:15.221
Three months later, all of the rabbit drawings
seemed to have vanished, with no clue if they

00:12:15.221 --> 00:12:20.709
had come from a child, or were created from
the town of SCP-277 itself.

00:12:20.709 --> 00:12:25.240
The local civilians gave mixed responses when
asked, some claiming to have no memory of

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:27.800
the event that put multiple children into
comas.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:32.379
Meanwhile, other townsfolk simply stated that
this sort of thing happens in Chalkland every

00:12:32.379 --> 00:12:33.589
few years.

00:12:33.589 --> 00:12:39.649
SCP Foundation staff noticed that the residents
of SCP-277 seemed to smile too wide when they

00:12:39.649 --> 00:12:46.149
explained this, as if their town was a fairytale,
and the massacre was just a part of a happy

00:12:46.149 --> 00:12:47.149
ending.

00:12:47.149 --> 00:12:51.249
Still, if you are thinking of stopping at
Chalkland, maybe it’s safer to just keep

00:12:51.249 --> 00:12:52.249
driving.

00:12:52.249 --> 00:12:57.149
Now go check out “You'll NEVER Make It To
SCP-084 - Static Tower” and “The Horror

00:12:57.149 --> 00:13:02.809
of Body Stealing Rain - SCP-3300” for more
places you should definitely avoid on your

00:13:02.809 --> 00:13:03.379
next road trip!

